SKEW — which two lanes the check reads at a wrong bit alignment

  The check reads bit 0 as F and bit 8 as S.  At skew d it reads
  bit d as F and bit (d+8) mod 16 as S.

   skew    as F    as S  what
      0       F       S  true alignment
      1      C0      C7  two payload lanes, eight seats apart
      2      C1      K0  payload or overhead, eight seats apart
      3      C2      K1  payload or overhead, eight seats apart
      4      C3      K2  payload or overhead, eight seats apart
      5      C4      K3  payload or overhead, eight seats apart
      6      C5      K4  payload or overhead, eight seats apart
      7      C6      K5  payload or overhead, eight seats apart
      8       S       F  header on itself
      9      C7      C0  two payload lanes, eight seats apart
     10      K0      C1  payload or overhead, eight seats apart
     11      K1      C2  payload or overhead, eight seats apart
     12      K2      C3  payload or overhead, eight seats apart
     13      K3      C4  payload or overhead, eight seats apart
     14      K4      C5  payload or overhead, eight seats apart
     15      K5      C6  payload or overhead, eight seats apart

  Eight C plus F and S opposite cannot avoid every C-C pair at
  distance 8: (C0, C7) are bits 1 and 9.  Overhead occupies the
  other six partners.  Header-on-itself is skew 8.

GUARD POSITION — 16-state superframe

  0 and 8 are half a superframe, both even.  A period-2 lane fails
  0,8 = 0,1.  256 hook states × 16 skews = 4096 per cell.

  layout                                 F word every  one data, worst   idle every  voice 4-run
  0,8 = 0,1  (family analogue)               0 / 4096         0 / 4096     0 / 4096     1 in 666
  0,8 = 1,0                                  0 / 4096         0 / 4096     0 / 4096     1 in 400
  0,7 = 0,1  (odd, analogue of 0,5)          0 / 4096         0 / 4096     0 / 4096     1 in 266
  0,4 = 0,1                                  0 / 4096         0 / 4096     0 / 4096     1 in 500
  0,8 = F word there                       512 / 4096       256 / 4096     0 / 4096     1 in 400

  0xFFFE is 1 at states 0 and 8, so the F word fails 0,8 = 0,1.

SLOT RULES — 16-bit frame, S at bit 8, word 0xFFFE, guard 0,8 = 0,1

  Payload seats C0..C7 at bits 1-7 and 9.  The only payload pair
  eight wire-bits apart is (C0, C7).

  1. PCM octets, every seat, then F word vs every octet in another.

